## Run the site

```sh title="Terminal"
go run ./cmd/gx dev
```

Open the address that the command prints. Edit this file and save. The page
updates in place.

<docs.Aside kind={docs.Tip}>
`go run ./cmd/gx check` finds a broken link, a bad frontmatter key and an
unknown component before you publish.
</docs.Aside>

## Add a page

Add a Markdown file to `content/docs`. The file path is the address of the
page: `content/docs/guides/install.md` is `/guides/install/`.

## Publish

```sh title="Terminal"
go run ./cmd/gx export --out dist
```

The `dist` directory holds static files. Any static host can serve them.
Read [the first guide](/guides/write-a-page/) next.
